## 9. The generated-ensemble campaign: infrastructure and pilot (§3 phase 3, item 01)

*loop0002 iteration 1, 2026-09-26. C

Final checks, all independent: the tick in iterations.md, that only the ensemble directory is exposed under `learning/data`, and that the CLI still parses.
  > $ grep -n "^- \[x\] 01\|^- \[ \] 02" Ralph_Loops/loop0002/iterations.md; git status --short --untracked-files=all learning/ reports/ .gitignore tests/ | grep -v "

Item 01 is done. Everything the driver needs is on disk, nothing was committed, and nothing touched `solutions/`.

**What was built.** `learning/ensemble.py` generates cells of `(generator, n, m, density)` under both generators, seeds each instance by a CRC of its cell and index so it regenerates byte for byte, solves it into `learning/data/ensemble/solutions/`, and records per instance the optimum and proof kind, witness re-simulation, nodes and seconds to refute `optimum − 1` under both search configurations, all 49 features, the isomorphism certificates and the component count. One CSV row per instance, resumable. The `.gitignore` now un-ignores `learning/data/ensemble/`.

**What the pilot found.** The specified pilot of 360 instances took 12 s, so I extended it to m = 2n, p = 0.025 and 100 per cell: 8,000 instances in 126 s on 16 workers. The audit is clean on every instance. The cost premise was wrong at these sizes: refuting `optimum − 1` is 0.7% of the time, and seconds are a smooth function of n alone while nodes vary by three orders of magnitude across density at fixed n = 40. Compute does not bind item 02, storage does, so the artifact is a manifest plus witnesses plus results (8.2 MB), with `.mosp` files opt-in. All 8,000 manifest rows regenerate with zero mismatches.

**The grid chosen for item 02.** Seven sizes from 10 to 40, m in {n, 2n}, d from 2 to 10, nine values of p from 0.025 to 0.5, 150 per cell. That is 37,800 instances, about six minutes of wall clock and about 40 MB. The reasoning and the previews for items 03 and 04 are in `reports/ml_nature.md` §9.

**Tests.** Six new tests in `tests/test_ensemble.py`, including the byte-for-byte regeneration and a hand-checked 4×4 instance with optimum 2 and a positive node count. Full suite: 782 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed in 75 s.

PROGRESS.md carries the iteration entry and reads 1/6 solved; item 01 is ticked in iterations.md.

